course: dictionary
lesson: 9156
title: Snorkel: breathing under water
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A snorkel is a short, bent tube. One end goes in your mouth and the other end sticks up above the water, so you can breathe while your face is under the surface. «Elephants swim well, using the trunk held above the water like a snorkel.» The words held above the water are the clue: the trunk is used to breathe, not to dig or to hold things.
explain: Snorkel can also be a verb. «When you snorkel the water looks blue» tells you that snorkel is something you do, so it means to swim with a snorkel and a mask. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? In this sentence, snorkel must be a doing word.
explain: Look at the words around the new word. «Mangroves grow breathing roots like snorkels» tells you that breathing is what a snorkel is for. When you are not sure, try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: A snorkel is a short, bent tube that lets you breathe while your face is in the water.
fact: To snorkel means to swim with a snorkel and a mask to look at fish and coral.
fact: People often snorkel on beaches and reefs, such as the Great Barrier Reef in Australia.
fact: «Mask and snorkel» and «go snorkelling» are common phrases.
fact: Submarines also have snorkels, so they can take in air while they are under water.
exercise: «Elephants swim well, using the trunk held above the water like a snorkel.» What is a snorkel in this sentence? | *A tube that lets you breathe while your face is under water | A type of boat | A long, soft ear for hearing fish | A kind of swimming costume
exercise: «Tapirs ... can work as a snorkel» What job does a snorkel do for a tapir? | Makes it swim faster than a fish | Helps it grab leaves faster | *Helps it breathe while its body is under water | Keeps it warm in the cold
exercise: Find and copy the word in this sentence that means swimming under water with a snorkel: «Liam wants to go snorkelling this summer.» | wants | this | *snorkelling | summer
test: «When you snorkel the water looks blue, and the deeper you go the darker it gets.» Why does it get darker? | Fish turn the water dark | The mask makes the water dark | *Less sunlight reaches deeper water | Snorkels cover the sun
test: Which sentence is true about a snorkel? | It is a kind of fish | It is a large sea animal | It is only a type of mask | *It is a short, bent tube for breathing
exam: Why do safety lessons teach children to snorkel with an adult, in calm water? | *Because it is safer, and children should never go deep with a snorkel | Because adults are better at breathing | Because snorkels only work with adults | Because calm water has more fish
